output.write_text('''<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Complete golf visual inspection</title><style>body{background:#13222b;color:#e5eeed;font:15px system-ui;margin:28px}h1{margin:0 0 8px}p{color:#b5caca;line-height:1.6}section{border-top:1px solid #46616c;margin:30px 0;padding:18px 0}.shots{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:14px}figure{margin:0;background:#213541;padding:10px}figcaption{margin:0 0 8px;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.1em}img{width:100%;height:300px;object-fit:contain;background:#10181d}.missing{height:300px;display:grid;place-items:center;color:#a1a7ad;border:1px dashed #5c636d}@media(max-width:850px){.shots{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}}</style></head><body><h1>Complete golf environment inspection</h1><p>Actual Unity captures from '''+html.escape(str(folder.relative_to(root)))+'''. GPT Image concepts remain comparison targets, and are not proof. A complete set of photos does not automatically establish visual quality, physics parity, phone performance or completion. Open a photo to inspect its full resolution.</p>'''+''.join(sections)+'''<section><h2>GalleryHero4 · actual audience acceptance</h2><p>Parent accepted all seven near/far/cheering face sheets: solid shirts, necks and grounded feet. A small close armpit cloth crease is accepted crowd detail. Actual production uses four rigid pieces per fan and zero skins, animators or colliders. Final integrated all19 synchronous dressing-physics and completed-frame editor draw gates PASS; peak214 calls and2,000,738 triangles including shadow/render passes. Phone frame time and final main-hero art remain separate.</p><div class="shots">'''+''.join(f'<figure><figcaption>{label}</figcaption><a href="{path}"><img loading="lazy" src="{path}"></a></figure>' for label,path in [('Near cheer','gallery4-near-cheer-all7.png'),('Far cheer ·18 yards','gallery4-far-cheer-all7.png'),('Cheering faces','gallery4-cheer-faces-all7.png')])+'''</div></section></body></html>''')
(output.parent/'catalog-capture-matrix.json').write_text(json.dumps(matrix,indent=2));print(json.dumps({'review':str(output),'captured_holes':sum(x['captured_shots']==6 for x in matrix),'holes':len(matrix)},indent=2))
